WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.940
Good morning Hank it's Friday, I'm going to do Alex Day's Youtube survey, but quickly four things

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:03.580
First:

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.240
Balls, balls, balls, ball, b-b-b-b-balls

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.120
Balls, balls, balls, balls, balls, b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:09.860
Balls, balls!

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.860
You said "balls" a lot in your last video

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.360
Second: Team 6 for life!

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.880
Third: our secret sister, Maureen Johnson, aka Actual John Green

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.020
had her best book ever: The Name of the Star come out yesterday

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.180
I am very excited about this book because everybody is gonna love it!

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.240
Fourth: Hank, did you know that Nerdfighters have loaned more than $55,000

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.600
to entrepreneurs in the developing world through Kiva?

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.320
French the Llama! $55,000!

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.080
Hank, I am once again reminded that Nerdfighters are made of awesome

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.240
So, every year Alex Day does a survey- well, this is the first year, but it's you know, gonna be every year

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.900
"Tell us about your first kiss"

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:42.800
I assume you mean French kiss

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.340
In that case, it was at summer camp

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.700
Summer camp was kinda like the internet before the internet was the internet

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.140
Like, at summer camp you were cooler and better looking

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.040
Than you were in were irl

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.660
Hank, you might have heard this story before

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.220
but I had a girlfriend, her name was Tiffany,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.460
and we had a candlelight ceremony

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.920
on the last night of camp.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.460
Hank, looking back I'm not even sure I would call it kissing;

00:00:58.460 --> 00:00:59.620
It was kinda like facial-licking.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:01.220
But anyway, we had this candelight ceremony

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.960
And we both knew that we wanted to French,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.480
we'd discussed it previously.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.000
Everybody's crying cause camp about to end,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.320
you gotta go back to your irl life where you aren't nearly as cool

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.540
And I walk up to Tiffany and I wrap my arms around her

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.480
and I start just you know,

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:14.540
licking her face

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:16.480
And, uh, eventually

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.740
I start to smell the fact that my hair is on fire

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.260
because I got my arm so far wrapped around her

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.940
the candle is like, lighting my hair

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.280
and it's burning

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.620
and... yeah.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.960
My second kiss, came three years later

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.120
"Most expensive casual item of clothing every bought"

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.660
Definitely this suit, which I had to buy so I wouldn't look like a dumb*ss

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.440
standing next to my wife at the Venice biennale.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.620
Of course, Hank, some will say that this suit isn't casual

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:41.300
in which case, my most expensive article of causal clothing

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.520
is probably my Team 6 for life t-shirt

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.900
"What was the first job you ever wanted as a kid?"

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:46.880
I don't know remember this Hank,

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:49.400
but when we were little, I really wanted an earthworm scientist

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.180
like a professional studier of earthworms

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.100
I guess because it mixed my two talents of animal husbandry and science

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.860
"Tell us about your group of school friends!"

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:00.320
I was a nerd, but for my last three years of high school, I went to a really nerdy boarding school

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.400
and there I wasn't really a nerd

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.520
I was kinda like, a trouble-maker.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:08.420
I'm so embarrassed to have this secret, non-nerdy past!

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.460
"What would you name your kids?"

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.140
How do you know you're too old for Youtube?

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.520
You've already named a kid.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.460
I really wanted to name Henry "Gatsby,"

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:19.000
but then Sarah was like "We can't name our child "Gatsby"!"

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.320
She was like, "He's a tragic character; you don't want our child to end up like Gatsby!"

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.180
But I was like, "No, no! Gatsby turned out all right at the end;

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:29.940
it is what preyed on Gatsby, what foul dust trailed in the wake of his dreams"

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.100
I actually wanted to put that quote over his crib.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.160
"Who do you want to answer the survey next?"

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.440
Everybody can leave survey responses here or at Nerimon's video

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.400
but I really want my brother

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.700
to answer the survey, my brother, Hank Green, whom I will see on Monday!

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.360
[singsong] My chair's so spinny, it's a spinny, spinny chair!

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:51.900
I promised Nerdfighteria I wouldn't sing anymore

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:52.438
[normal voice] I'm sorry

